        "parms": "# programchange, channelpressure and polypressure — programs and pressure out\nprogramchange tells a synthesizer to switch to another sound, its program. channelpressure sends aftertouch for a whole channel, and polypressure for one key. Each builds a message for midiout and sends it from the left inlet. Their argument is the channel, counted from 0. midiout's argument is the output port, counted from 0; the midiinfo tutorial lists them. You hear something only when a synthesizer listens on that port.\nProgram change and channel pressure have one data byte, so their message is two bytes long, such as 192 5. Before libYSE 3.0.1 a zero byte was added after it.\nMax's pgmout numbers programs 1-128. Here programchange takes the number as it goes on the wire, 0-127: a synthesizer that counts from 1 shows 6 for 5.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
